<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Annotations by Pablo Caro - security</title><link href="/en/" rel="alternate"></link><link href="/en/feeds/tags/security.atom.xml" rel="self"></link><id>/en/</id><updated>2026-05-28T00:00:00+02:00</updated><subtitle>Anotaciones</subtitle><entry><title>Detecting secrets in git with gitleaks</title><link href="/en/gitleaks-deteccion-secrets-git" rel="alternate"></link><published>2026-05-28T00:00:00+02:00</published><updated>2026-05-28T00:00:00+02:00</updated><author><name>Pablo Caro</name></author><id>tag:None,2026-05-28:/en/gitleaks-deteccion-secrets-git</id><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;gitleaks scans git repositories for secrets, API keys, and leaked credentials. Install it in seconds with gah — it might save you from a very bad day.&lt;/p&gt;</summary><content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="gitleaks detecting secrets in a git repo" src="/images/gitleaks-deteccion-secrets-git.png"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;gitleaks&lt;/code&gt; scans git repositories —including the full commit history— for secrets: API keys, passwords, AWS tokens, database credentials, and over 150 predefined patterns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="installing-with-gah"&gt;Installing with gah&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#installing-with-gah" title="Permanent link"&gt;&amp;para;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The fastest way on Linux is with &lt;a href="https://github.com/user/gah"&gt;&lt;code&gt;gah&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, a GitHub release asset downloader:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;$&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;gah&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;install&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;gitleaks/gitleaks
Fetching&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;release&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;info&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;gitleaks/gitleaks&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;latest&lt;span class="o"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
Found&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;release:&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;v8.30.1
Downloading:&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;gitleaks_8.30.1_linux_x64.tar.gz
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;############################################### 100.0%&lt;/span&gt;
Verifying&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;digest&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;sha256&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;551f6fc8...&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;...
Digest&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;verification&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;succeeded!
Extracting:&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;gitleaks_8.30.1_linux_x64.tar.gz
Installing:&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;gitleaks
Done!
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Single binary, zero dependencies, ready in seconds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="basic-usage"&gt;Basic usage&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#basic-usage" title="Permanent link"&gt;&amp;para;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To scan a local repo with full commit history:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;$&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;gitleaks&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;git&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;--verbose&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;-v&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;/path/to/repo
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It walks every commit and shows what secrets it found, in which file and at which line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Some useful flags:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;--no-banner&lt;/code&gt;: hides the ASCII banner at startup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;--exit-code 0&lt;/code&gt;: don't exit with error when leaks are found (handy for CI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;--config .gitleaks.toml&lt;/code&gt;: use a custom config with your own detection rules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;--gitleaks-ignore-path .&lt;/code&gt;: respects the &lt;code&gt;.gitleaksignore&lt;/code&gt; file for false positives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;--redact&lt;/code&gt;: masks secrets in output (useful for public logs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can also scan standalone directories with &lt;code&gt;gitleaks dir&lt;/code&gt; or pipe content through &lt;code&gt;gitleaks stdin&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="when-to-use-it"&gt;When to use it&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#when-to-use-it" title="Permanent link"&gt;&amp;para;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Before making a repo public&lt;/strong&gt;: scan the full history to make sure no keys slipped through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In CI/CD&lt;/strong&gt;: add it as a GitHub Actions step so the build fails if someone commits a secret.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security audits&lt;/strong&gt;: great for reviewing old repos that have been touched by many people.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="pre-commit-hook"&gt;Pre-commit hook&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#pre-commit-hook" title="Permanent link"&gt;&amp;para;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The most effective way to use it is as a &lt;a href="https://github.com/BadLiveware/pi/blob/main/.githooks/pre-commit"&gt;pre-commit hook&lt;/a&gt; that automatically blocks any commit containing secrets:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="ch"&gt;#!/usr/bin/env bash&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;-euo&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;pipefail

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;[[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;SKIP_GITLEAKS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;:-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;SKIP_GITLEAKS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;:-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;quot;true&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;]]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="w"&gt;  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;echo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;quot;Skipping gitleaks pre-commit scan because SKIP_GITLEAKS=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;SKIP_GITLEAKS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;.&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="w"&gt;  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;exit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;fi&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;!&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;command&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;-v&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;gitleaks&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt;/dev/null&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="w"&gt;  &lt;/span&gt;cat&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;lt;&amp;#39;EOF&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s"&gt;gitleaks is required by this repository&amp;#39;s pre-commit hook but was not found.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s"&gt;Install gitleaks, or set SKIP_GITLEAKS=1 for an intentional one-off bypass.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="s"&gt;EOF&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="w"&gt;  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;exit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;fi&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nb"&gt;echo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;quot;Running gitleaks on staged changes...&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;
gitleaks&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;protect&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;--staged&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;--source&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;--redact&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;--no-banner
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Save this as &lt;code&gt;.githooks/pre-commit&lt;/code&gt;, make it executable (&lt;code&gt;chmod +x&lt;/code&gt;), and configure git to use that directory:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code&gt;git&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;config&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;core.hooksPath&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;.githooks
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;From then on, every &lt;code&gt;git commit&lt;/code&gt; will scan staged changes for secrets. Need to bypass it once? &lt;code&gt;SKIP_GITLEAKS=1 git commit&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It's one of those tools you don't need until you &lt;em&gt;really&lt;/em&gt; need it. And when that day comes, you'll be glad it's just a &lt;code&gt;gah install&lt;/code&gt; away.&lt;/p&gt;</content><category term="tools"></category><category term="git"></category><category term="security"></category><category term="gitleaks"></category><category term="tools"></category><category term="cli"></category></entry></feed>